The fluid mechanics of aerosols — Goodarz Ahmadi, Clarkson (@cm-ahmadi-source: 0, is #reference, #part-of @cm-sources) { r_175C6Q2GTKPZJJ6XSRHF5979G0
Goodarz Ahmadi, Clarkson University. *ME537: The Fluid Mechanics of Aerosols*. [Course notes and downloads](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/courses/me537/course-notes/) · [Syllabus](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/courses/me537/syllabus/). The notes are undated; a 2020 upload path is not proof of their publication date.

Read the available engineering mathematics, viscous-flow and aerosol notes as a sustained course, followed by adhesion, measurement and applications. For this section read Hydrodynamic Forces (11 pages), Aerosol Particle Motion (5), Brownian Motion (12), Mass Diffusion (12), Diffusion to a Cylinder (7), Coagulation of Particles (17), Electrostatics (3) and Inertia Impactions (5). Some course headings have no download; some linked files carry ME437/537 or ME637 labels. A listed topic is not proof that its complete material is supplied.

The course index and those eight PDFs were inspected in selected passages on 30 October 2026. Drag/slip, Brownian correlation and coagulation-counting pages were also viewed visually; the coagulation PDF has missing displayed glyphs. Assigned full reading is broader than this inspection. Institutional reading access is free; no blanket adaptation licence was verified, and figures have external credits. Keep source media external.


Continue with [London–van der Waals forces, seven pages](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2020/06/ME537-5_vanderWaals.pdf), [Particle adhesion and detachment models, seven pages](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2020/06/ME537-6_JKR.pdf), [Rough-particle removal, six pages](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2020/06/ME537-8_rough.pdf) and [Bumpy-particle removal, ten pages](https://sites.clarkson.edu/gahmadi/wp-content/uploads/sites/28/2020/06/ME537-9_bumpy.pdf). [Particle–substrate interactions — Don Rimai, edited by Goodarz Ahmadi](Particle-Substrate-Interactions-Rimai.lingua#r_67MEFYZ26RD2ERAEKSVC0ACCQM) preserves the separate authorship of the two companion presentations.

Selected energy, contact, roughness and removal passages were inspected on 30 October 2026. Dispersion page 4 and adhesion-model pages 1 and 3 were viewed visually: some equations contain missing glyphs or lose radicals during extraction. Model conventions were reconciled with the Rimai presentation and independent algebra. Tables, removal correlations and every plotted result were not independently reproduced. Complete reading remains assigned; figures and PDFs stay external.

